    "show_share": true,
    "description": "As the world races to meet the ambitious goal of conserving 30% of the planet by 2030, community-led conservation is increasingly seen as a promising solution. But why do so many of these initiatives struggle to grow and succeed? A  new study  published in  Conservation Biology  offers some answers.",
